WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.334
-Adam, you're getting
a standing ovation here,

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.133
even though you're on Zoom.
-Yep.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.834
-That's --
Oh, you love --

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.934
-Come on. Give me as much
as you gave Anthony.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Unbelievable.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.734
Unbelievable.
[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:16.934
Oh, you're the best, buddy.
I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.200
Thank you so much
for doing the show.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.067
I appreciate it.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.767
Thanks, man.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:24.734
I also got the omicron, so...
-Did you really?

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.400
-That's why I'm here, or else
I'd be in studio with you.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.534
-Wow. How are you feeling
with the omicron?

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:33.200
-I feel...stronger.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:39.367
It gave me the adverse effects.
-Wow!

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.901
-I don't know -- no.
I'm gonna get a call from Fauci.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.467
I can't be spreading
that information.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:45.567
It was the same thing.
I was sick for like three days.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.501
-Yeah.
-But I'm back now, baby.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.400
-Yeah, I'm happy your back.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.901
You look good.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.300
-And thank you for doing this.
I wanted to say congratulations

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.400
to you, because you
recently got married.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.601
That's a big deal.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:58.234
-Oh, this little thing?
-Whoa! Look at that.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:00:59.334
Look at the ring.

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:01.634
♪♪

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.968
How did you and your wife meet?

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:07.801
-It's a real meet cute, Jimmy.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.734
We actually met on a plane.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.834
-Wow.
-Ooh! Yeah.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.467
We were shooting the same movie,
but I didn't know that

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.667
because I'm an idiot
who doesn't read e-mails.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.300
I just -- like, they just
pushed me onto an airplane.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.634
And I'm like,
"Where am I going?"

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:22.801
They're like,
"You're shooting a movie."

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:25.834
I'm like, "Okay."
But Chloe is a smart person

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:28.701
who reads e-mails,
and she knew who I was.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.000
And so, she's, like,
trying to chat me up.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.000
And, meanwhile, I just think,
"This babe is hitting on me."

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:37.734
And I was like
a little overwhelmed.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.667
I had a girlfriend at the time.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.567
I'm like,
"I don't want any of this.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.934
I don't know.
I get it.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:45.334
I'm charming."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:48.167
-Oh, my gosh.
-And then, we land,

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:51.000
and I realize
we had the same driver

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.634
to take us from New Orleans
to Baton Rouge.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.467
And I'm like,
"Oh, you're in the movie!"

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:56.634
She's like,
"Yeah. What did you think?"

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.567
I'm like, "No, no, I knew.
I knew you were."

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.167
[ Laughter ]
And we're driving,

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:04.567
and she goes, "Should we get
some drive-through daiquiris?"

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.567
Which is a thing
you can do in New Orleans.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.567
There's a drive-through
daiquiri place.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.000
I know -- it's great.
[ Cheers ]

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.567
And she's -- I'm like,
"Well, what size?"

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.501
I didn't want to, like,
get too big of a size and,

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.200
you know, be like,
"Oh, is this guy a drunk?"

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.968
So, but she ordered first,
and she's like,

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.567
"I'll take
the 48-ounce party starter."

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:23.767
And I was like --
-You're like,

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.300
"Will you marry me?"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.801
-"Will you marry me?"
-"Will you marry me?

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.834
Who are you?"
Unicorn.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:32.367
-You know what?
The time is now.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:35.534
-Congratulations.
I know that you're gonna do a --

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.534
you're doing
a "Pitch Perfect" series.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:39.634
I know.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.300
We love the movie.
-Yeah.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.901
-Based around your character.
What can you say about it?

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:46.901
I know you're not filming it
yet, but is it happening soon?

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:49.767
What can you say?
It --

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:52.467
Essentially, it takes place
around my character

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:55.834
after the second movie,
and Bumper goes on "The Voice,"

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.901
and you think his career
is gonna skyrocket.

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:02.701
But he releases an album, and it
totally tanks here in America.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.367
And he runs into some German
tourists and they're like,

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:07.934
"Oh, my God,
you're huge in Germany.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.734
Like, you have a song
that's a hit."

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.734
So then,
Bumper packs up his stuff

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.801
and goes to Germany to try
to make it as a pop sensation.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.100
-That's fantastic.
-Which is...

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.834
-I will love that.
-...when you're nearing 40

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:23.200
is when --
is when your pop stardom

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.067
really starts to peak, I feel.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.334
Let's talk about
"Righteous Gemstones."

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:31.934
Very funny. Season two premieres
this Sunday at 10:00 p.m.

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:34.167
on HBO and HBO Max.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:37.167
Dude, it's so funny.
Everyone's so good in this.

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:39.801
But you get to really go off
and play --

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:43.000
Kelvin is your character.
-That's right.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.934
-Some of your outfits,
I just chose some of them

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:49.667
just to show what
your character dresses like.

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.367
This is from that past season.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.367
It's fashionable.
-Yeah, he's pretty chill.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.801
-Yeah, I would say chill, yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:01.667
-I feel like
I realize that I just recently

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.467
learned the word "cheugy."

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.133
Do you know
what the word "cheugy" means?

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.300
-Yes, cheugy.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.467
I'm cheugy.
-Yes! Oh, my gosh!

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:13.834
Kelvin is cheugy.
-All of Kelvin's outfits

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.300
are cheugy, which is like
you're trying too hard

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.534
or you're like -- you have
something that maybe

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:23.267
was cool in the past
and no longer isn't cool at all.

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:26.767
That's what I am, both as
a person and as an actor.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.601
-No, no, no,
your character is cheugy.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.100
Well, we love you, buddy.
You're always so fun.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.267
Thank you so much.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:34.133
And hopefully next time
in person, okay?

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:35.601
-Absolutely.
Good to see you, guys.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Best to your wife.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.501
-Thank you.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:42.400
Here's Adam Devine
in "The Righteous Gemstones."

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.901
Take a look at this.

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:46.234
♪♪

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.133
-Let's not fill up
on rolls here.

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.367
Stick to the salad bar.
Don't forget --

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:55.100
we are swimming laps
after lunch, so eat light.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.701
We nourish our bodies
for his love.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.868
Coo'.
-So cool.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:06.501
-Excuse me, sir.
-What's up?

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.868
Dismissed.
-It's just...

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:11.033
Will you be dining
with the men and I?

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:13.033
